// ## 3. OCap bridge coverage of the 20 NORTHSTAR language tokens

// Per NORTHSTAR §1.4 the canonical surface is 20 language tokens.
// All 20 are now backed by OCap records in ocap_to_oodar.oo:

// | #  | Language token  | Rights mask | Bits used         |
// |---:|-----------------|------------:|-------------------|
// |  1 | FsReadCap       |           1 | read              |
// |  2 | FsWriteCap      |           3 | read + write      |
// |  3 | NetCap          |           3 | read + write      |
// |  4 | TcpCap          |           3 | read + write      |
// |  5 | UdpCap          |           3 | read + write      |
// |  6 | SysCap          |           7 | read + write + exec |
// |  7 | ProcessCap      |           7 | read + write + exec |
// |  8 | EnvCap          |           1 | read              |
// |  9 | TimeCap         |           1 | read              |
// | 10 | RandCap         |           1 | read              |
// | 11 | AllocCap        |           3 | read + write      |
// | 12 | ThreadCap       |           7 | read + write + exec |
// | 13 | GpuCap          |           7 | read + write + exec |
// | 14 | FfiCap          |           7 | read + write + exec |
// | 15 | FsCap           |          31 | full authority    |
// | 16 | ArenaCap        |          11 | read + write + delegate |
// | 17 | MetricsCap      |           1 | read              |
// | 18 | SignCap         |           3 | read + write      |
// | 19 | BindCap         |           3 | read + write      |
// | 20 | CompilerReadCap |           1 | read              |

// Coverage is complete. The 26 substrate caps in oodar's
// g_tok_* all map to one of the 20 language tokens via the
// SUBSTRATE_TO_LANGUAGE[26] table in cap_ocap_bridge.c. The 6
// substrate-only caps (audio/camera/usb/hid/window/frame) all
// map to FsReadCap for now per the substrate convention.

// Verification: qa/tests_challenger_ocap_bridge.c (oodar,
// 332 lines, 6 hostile probes including a table-driven probe 6
// that exercises all 22 oo_cap_require_* gates × 2 passes
// = 44 forks total). 6/6 PASS in the v4.5.0 release.

// ## 4. Cross-repo consumer pattern

// `ocap_to_oodar.oo` is the canonical example of a cross-repo
// bridge shim:
//
//   std/sec/capability/ocap_to_oodar.oo  (source of truth, .oo)
//        |
//        |  oodac emit-c (Makefile emit-std-ocap target)
//        v
//   oodar/sec/cap/cap_bridge_emitted.c  (gitignored, build artifact)
//        |
//        |  #include in oodar.c
//        v
//   oodar/sec/cap/cap_ocap_bridge.c     (the C bridge)
//        |
//        v
//   oodar/sec/cap/cap_require.c         (the 22 cap gates)

// Volume-cert classification under the std-only audit sees 0
// callers in std/, which by the strict rule would be BLOCKED.
// The actual consumer (oodar) is outside the audit's scope.
//
// Resolution: classify as RESIDUAL with a cross-repo consumer
// note in the CSV. The audit framework should add a 6th status
// "CROSS-REPO" in a future revision to handle this pattern
// explicitly. Defer the audit-framework change to a follow-up
// session.

// ## 5. Recommended next actions

// 1. Update ANCHOR.oo's "Private sibling inventory" comment to
